"Every computer and phone has a CPU, which is its main processor. A CPU follows a program one instruction at a time: it fetches an instruction, works out what it means, and carries it out. It does this billions of times a second. A CPU can do almost any kind of job, and modern ones have several cores, so they can do a few things at once.": "1c41dae1e5d6",
"Every computer and phone has a CPU, which is its main processor. A CPU follows a program one instruction at a time: it fetches an instruction, works out what it means, and carries it out. It does this billions of times a second. A CPU can do almost any kind of job, and modern ones have several cores, so they can do a few things at once. In the 1990s, video games gave computers a new kind of job. A picture on a screen is made of a huge number of pixels, and the color of every pixel must be calculated again and again. Each calculation is simple, and most of them do not depend on each other. So engineers built a different kind of chip for this work: the graphics processing unit, or GPU. A GPU does not have a few big cores. It has hundreds or thousands of small calculation units, and they all work at the same time. Think of painting a long wall. One expert painter is fast, but a thousand children, each with one small square to paint, will finish first. Doing many things at the same time is called working in parallel. Then scientists noticed something. AI programs called neural networks need the same kind of work: an enormous number of simple multiplications and additions. In 2012 a team in Toronto trained a neural network called AlexNet on two GPUs made for games. It won a famous contest for recognizing pictures, far ahead of the others. After that, GPUs became widely used for AI. Today some chips are designed only for AI. They are called AI accelerators or neural processing units, and many phones have one inside. But a crowd of small units is not always better. Some jobs must be done in order, because each step needs the answer from the step before. For those jobs, a fast CPU core still wins. So a computer that runs AI uses both kinds of chips. The CPU is the manager: it runs the program and decides what to do next. The GPU or AI chip is the crowd: it takes the big jobs that can be shared and finishes them quickly. Neither one is simply better. They are good at different things, and they work as a team.": "589688c85848",
